Here is the commit message:
Fix a bug introduced in ef133e4 where a system with
 OS_TIMER=0 would run into problems when the formats called
 sig_timer_emu_tick() during benchmark. To fix this, I made bench_running a
 global variable. Maybe there are better ways. This patch also fixes a minor
 bug in erasing the "spinning wheel".

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the `sig_timer_emu_tick()` function being called during benchmarking when `OS_TIMER` is set to 0, which led to issues in systems where the timer emulation was not properly managed. This was exacerbated by the `bench_running` variable being static, preventing it from being accessed correctly across different files, thus allowing the timer function to execute at inappropriate times.

